<title>NETHERLANDS: Aegon unit FGH posts lower '96 net profit.</title>
<headline>Aegon unit FGH posts lower '96 net profit.</headline>
<dateline>THE HAGUE 1997-04-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Yr to Dec 31, 1996</p>
<p>(in millions of guilders unless otherwise stated)</p>
<p>    Net profit			    85    vs 105</p>
<p>    Gross income			 115    vs 140</p>
<p>    Tax				     26    vs  30</p>
<p>    Loan loss provisions		 4    vs   5</p>
<p>    New mortgage production (bln)    2.17 vs   2.02</p>
<p>    Total portfolio (billion)	  5.70 vs   5.54</p>
<p>NOTE - FGH Bank NV, a mortgage bank owned by insurer Aegon NV, previously said it expected the 1996 profit to fall because of a financial reorganisation.</p>
<p>The company has replaced about 550 million guilders' worth of non-interest bearing liabilities with interest bearing debt. This had caused an extra interest charge of 24.5 million guilders in 1997, it said.</p>
<p>FGH said it expected the 1997 net result to be in the same region as last year's figure.</p>
<p>-- Amsterdam newsroom +31 20 504 5000, Fax +31 20 504 5040</p>
